00:57:07.000 --> 00:57:09.000
A child is unable to describe things outside

00:57:09.000 --> 00:57:11.000
him.

00:57:11.000 --> 00:57:13.000
The first words of a child

00:57:13.000 --> 00:57:15.000
always have things to do with his own person.

00:57:15.000 --> 00:57:17.000
He doesn't even... A child,

00:57:17.000 --> 00:57:19.000
when he...

00:57:19.000 --> 00:57:21.000
Psychologists today say something, which is very important.

00:57:21.000 --> 00:57:23.000
Why a child

00:57:23.000 --> 00:57:25.000
does not,

00:57:25.000 --> 00:57:27.000
cannot speak

00:57:27.000 --> 00:57:29.000
when he's, say, you know, very young?

00:57:29.000 --> 00:57:31.000
Because he doesn't hear.

00:57:31.000 --> 00:57:33.000
He doesn't hear because he only thinks of, you know,

00:57:33.000 --> 00:57:35.000
he doesn't pay attention to what is

00:57:35.000 --> 00:57:37.000
outside his own self.

00:57:37.000 --> 00:57:39.000
A child

00:57:39.000 --> 00:57:41.000
doesn't speak, for instance,

00:57:41.000 --> 00:57:43.000
when a child speaks,

00:57:43.000 --> 00:57:45.000
mispronounces a word. It's not because he's unable

00:57:45.000 --> 00:57:47.000
to pronounce correctly.

00:57:47.000 --> 00:57:49.000
Because he doesn't hear well.

00:57:49.000 --> 00:57:51.000
And why doesn't he hear well? Because he doesn't want to pay attention.

00:57:51.000 --> 00:57:53.000
It's all things.

00:57:53.000 --> 00:57:55.000
He's not concentrating.

00:57:55.000 --> 00:57:57.000
He's not concentrating. In other words,

00:57:57.000 --> 00:57:59.000
what psychologists today show is that

00:57:59.000 --> 00:58:01.000
mispronunciation, when, you know,

00:58:01.000 --> 00:58:03.000
a child always mispronounces, you know,

00:58:03.000 --> 00:58:05.000
